From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kaput}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*káput}}. [[cognate|Cognates]] include {{cog|de|Haupt}} and {{cog|en|head}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|caput/capit<3.N>}}

# The [[head]]. {{q|of [[human]] and [[animal]]s}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''caput''' {{l|la|hūmānum}}|t=human head}}
## {{lb|la|poetic}} The [[head]] as the [[seat]] of the [[understanding]].
# {{lb|la|transferred sense}} {{q|of [[inanimate]] things}}:
## {{q|in general}} The [[head]], [[top]], [[summit]], [[point]], [[end]], [[extremity]] ([[beginning]] or end).
##* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|4|354|thru=355|quote=“[...] mē puer Ascanius '''capitis'''que iniūria '''cārī''',<br/>quem rēgnō Hesperiae fraudō et fātālibus arvīs.”|trans=''“[I consider] my son Ascanius, and my wronging '''of his dear life’s summit''', [how] I deprive him of his Hesperian kingdom and destined fields.”''<br/>({{w|Ascanius}} will become a legendary king and ancestor of the {{w|gens Julia}}.)}}
## The [[origin]], [[source]], [[spring]] ([[head]]). {{q|of [[river]]s}}
##* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|1|1|quote=nunc ad aquae lēne '''caput''' sacrae.
|trans=now by some gentle river's sacred '''spring'''.}}
## {{lb|la|rare|of [[river]]s}} The [[mouth]], [[embouchure]].
## {{lb|la|botany|sometimes}} The [[root]].
## [[vine|Vine]] [[branch]]es.
## {{lb|la|poetic}} {{q|of [[tree]]s}} The [[summit]], [[top]].
#: {{uxi|la|'''caput''' {{l|la|rerum}}|t=the main point of the matter}}
# {{lb|la|literature}} A [[man]], [[person]], or [[animal]].
# {{lb|la|figurative}}:
## [[physical|Physical]] [[life]].
##* {{Q|la|Caesar|De Bello Gallico|VII|1|quote={{...}} omnibus pollicitationibus ac praemiis deposcunt qui belli initium faciant et sui '''capitis''' periculo Galliam in libertatem vindicent.
|trans=and by every sort of promises and rewards, they earnestly solicit some to begin the war, and assert the freedom of Gaul at the hazard of their '''lives'''.}}
## [[civil|Civil]] or [[political]] [[life]].
## {{lb|la|very|frequently}} The [[first]] or [[chief]] person or thing; the [[head]], [[leader]], [[chief]], [[guide]], [[capital]].
##* {{Q|la|Titus Livius|Ab Urbe Condita|1|16|quote=ut mea Rōma '''caput''' orbis terrārum sit
|trans=that my Rome shall be the '''capital''' of the world}}
##* {{Q|la|Titus Livius|Ab Urbe Condita|8|4|quote=quippe concēdentibus Rōmam '''caput''' Latiō esse
|trans=seeing that we acknowledge Rome to be the '''capital''' of Latium}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''capita''' {{l|la|rerum}}|t=the heads of the state affairs}}
# {{lb|la|writing}} A [[division]], [[section]], [[paragraph]], [[chapter]].
#: {{syn|la|capitulum}}
# {{lb|la|New Latin|anatomy}} A [[headlike]] [[protuberance]] on an [[organ]] or [[body]] part, usually [[bone]].
#: {{uxi|la|'''caput''' ulnae|'''head''' of the ulna}}
# {{lb|la|New Latin|disease}} A [[disease]]; a severe [[swelling]] of the [[soft tissue]]s of a [[newborn]]'s [[scalp]] that develops as the baby travels through the [[birth canal]].

====Usage notes====
* {{m|la||Caput}} can be used with either a genitive or a dative in the sense of a [[capital city]].

